{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates C++ code to Java 8 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following GNU C++ code to Java 8 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original GNU C++ code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <cmath>\nusing namespace std;\n\nlong long generate_ones(int digits) {\n    long long result = 0;\n    for (int i = 0; i < digits; ++i) {\n        result = result * 10 + 1;\n    }\n    return result;\n}\n\nint solve(long long n, int max_digits) {\n    if (max_digits == 0) return 0;\n    \n    long long repunit = generate_ones(max_digits);\n    int count = (n / repunit) * max_digits;\n    n %= repunit;\n    \n    if (n == 0) return count;\n    \n    int option1 = max_digits + solve(repunit - n, max_digits - 1);\n    int option2 = solve(n, max_digits - 1);\n    \n    return count + min(option1, option2);\n}\n\nint main() {\n    cout << solve(0, 0);\n    return 0;\n}\n\n// Note: This variant is incomplete as it hardcodes 0. Below is the corrected version:\n\n#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\nusing namespace std;\n\nvector<long long> precompute_ones() {\n    vector<long long> res(20);\n    res[0] = 0;\n    for (int i = 1; i <= 16; ++i) {\n        res[i] = res[i-1] * 10 + 1;\n    }\n    return res;\n}\n\nint count_ones(long long n, int i, const vector<long long>& ones) {\n    long long val = ones[i];\n    int times = (n / val) * i;\n    n %= val;\n    \n    if (n == 0) return times;\n    \n    int use_more = i + count_ones(val - n, i - 1, ones);\n    int skip_more = count_ones(n, i - 1, ones);\n    \n    return times + min(use_more, skip_more);\n}\n\nint main() {\n    auto ones = precompute_ones();\n    long long n;\n    cin >> n;\n    cout << count_ones(n, 16, ones) << '\\n';\n    return 0;\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner scanner = new Scanner(System.in);\n        long[] ones = precomputeOnes();\n        long n = scanner.nextLong();\n        System.out.println(countOnes(n, 16, ones));\n    }\n    \n    private static long[] precomputeOnes() {\n        long[] res = new long[20];\n        res[0] = 0;\n        for (int i = 1; i <= 16; ++i) {\n            res[i] = res[i-1] * 10 + 1;\n        }\n        return res;\n    }\n    \n    private static int countOnes(long n, int i, long[] ones) {\n        long val = ones[i];\n        int times = (int)(n / val) * i;\n        n %= val;\n        \n        if (n == 0) return times;\n        \n        int useMore = i + countOnes(val - n, i - 1, ones);\n        int skipMore = countOnes(n, i - 1, ones);\n        \n        return times + Math.min(useMore, skipMore);\n    }\n}\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-9.881961887003854e-05, -4.0531076592742465e-06, -3.576278118089249e-07, -0.00021479207498487085, -1.3828182090946939e-05, -0.00064876489341259, -0.11511873453855515, -2.9444261599564925e-05, -3.576278118089249e-07, -0.00010966652916977182, -0.007606353145092726, -0.2811596393585205, -0.30043452978134155, -1.311301275563892e-06, -0.554431140422821, -3.302042750874534e-05, -1.168244216387393e-05, -2.467601916578132